TWO POINTER:
    - Start with two pointers, one at the beginning of the string and one at the end.
    - Compare the characters at the two pointers.
    - If they are equal, move the pointers towards each other.
    - If they are not equal, return false.
    - If the pointers meet or pass each other, return true.
int n = palindrome.length();

int start = 0;
int end = n - 1;

while start is less than or equals to end:
    if palindrome.charAt(start) != palindrome.charAt(end):
        return false
    start++;
    end--;

return true
